# oracle: pair gayberne with fix nve/asphere, bit for bit (the first run of w79srd_ellipsoid: 9 big ellipsoids, shape 3 1 1, quat/random, 50 NVE steps, thermo every step)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-14 abs=1e-13 atomrel=1e-15
# Measured with native LAMMPS: the final positions, velocities and forces of every atom are identical, and every thermo value agrees to 4.6e-15 (the 15 printed digits). That needs each piece in native's operation order: set quat/random with glibc sin and cos (src/engine-gpl/libm), the pair_gayberne.cpp port with its pairs in native order, native's reverse_comm fold of the ghost forces and torques and its fdotr virial (NativeReverseComm in src/engine-gpl/neighbor/nativeOrder.ts), and MathExtra::richardson with the moments as INERTIA*rmass*(...) for fix nve/asphere. Before, the forces of three atoms differed by one ulp at step 0 (fold order) and the orientations from step 2 (Richardson update).
units		lj
atom_style	ellipsoid
atom_modify	first big
dimension	2

lattice		sq 0.14
region		box block 0 3 0 3 -0.5 0.5
create_box	2 box
create_atoms	1 region box
set		type 1 mass 1.0
set		type 1 shape 3.0 1.0 1.0
group		big type 1
set		group big quat/random 29898
velocity	big create 1.44 87287 loop geom

pair_style	gayberne 1.0 3.0 1.0 4.0
pair_coeff	1 1 1.0 1.0 1 1 1 1 1 1
pair_coeff	1 2 1.0 1.0 1 1 1 1 1 1 0.0
pair_coeff	2 2 1.0 1.0 1 1 1 1 1 1 0.0

neighbor	0.3 bin
neigh_modify	delay 0 every 1 check yes
fix		1 big nve/asphere
fix		2 all enforce2d
compute		rot big temp/asphere
thermo_style	custom step temp c_rot epair etotal press
thermo_modify	format float %.15g
thermo		1
run		50
